@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Phase 23 — Silver Bullet Research Model
+
+## Goal
+Add Silver Bullet as a deterministic setup family beside `SWEEP_MSS_FVG`, without changing the existing setup engine or granting the new family verdict authority.
+
+## Scope
+- XAUUSD-first, broker-independent research output.
+- M5 closed candles only.
+- America/New_York wall-clock windows, converted with IANA timezone rules:
+  - London: 03:00–04:00
+  - New York AM: 10:00–11:00
+  - New York PM: 14:00–15:00
+- Separate API: `GET /api/v1/silver-bullet/{symbol}`.
+- Verdict authority: `RESEARCH_ONLY`; the system-wide authority remains `FAIL_SAFE_ONLY`.
+- No live execution and no claim of profitability.
+
+## Deterministic Rules
+1. A classic FVG must become known inside one of the three windows. Formation at the exact end boundary is excluded.
+2. The FVG must meet the configured quality floor and reference a same-direction, causally known displacement of at least the configured grade.
+3. Entry is the FVG proximal edge. A fill can only occur on a later closed M5 candle and before the window ends.
+4. Invalidation is the latest causally known opposing swing, buffered by ATR. Missing or impossible stop geometry blocks the candidate.
+5. The target is the nearest causally known, untaken same-direction liquidity pool beyond entry. Missing target liquidity blocks the candidate.
+6. R:R below the configured minimum blocks the candidate.
+7. Target reached before retracement produces `ENTRY_MISSED`.
+8. A candle that can contain both entry and target, or entry and stop, is intrabar-ambiguous and therefore `BLOCKED`.
+9. A data gap between formation and entry/window end is `BLOCKED`, never silently treated as expiry.
+10. An unfilled candidate expires at the end of its own Silver Bullet window.
+
+## States
+- `ARMED`: valid geometry; waiting for retracement before the window end.
+- `FILLED`: a later closed M5 candle traded through the proximal edge.
+- `ENTRY_MISSED`: target liquidity was reached first.
+- `EXPIRED`: no retracement before the window ended.
+- `BLOCKED`: causal evidence, geometry, data integrity, or intrabar ordering is unsafe.
+
+## Configuration
+`packages/strategy-spec/silver_bullet.json` owns the windows and untuned research defaults. Any modification requires a strategy-version bump.
+
+## Tests
+- Winter/summer DST conversion.
+- Exact start/end boundaries.
+- Formation/fill causality.
+- Displacement, structural-stop, liquidity-target, and minimum-R:R gates.
+- Expiry, data gaps, target-before-entry, and intrabar ambiguity.
+- API separation, research-only authority, unknown symbol, and invalid bar count.
+
+## Known Limitations
+- Real XAUUSD historical data is not included in this clone, so no out-of-sample expectancy, profit factor, drawdown, or robustness claim is made here.
+- Filled-trade outcome simulation and walk-forward reporting are not yet connected to the existing backtest job system.
+- Source-video transcripts could not be retrieved from this server because YouTube blocked the cloud IP. Ambiguous Silver Bullet interpretations were not guessed; only explicit project rules were encoded as configurable behavior.
+
+## Strategy Version
+`0.23.0-phase23-silver-bullet-research`.
